Rollout patch 0005: make fused_gr_read_multi run on gfx1100 and diagnose its guard.
1. TILE 2560 -> 1024: the multi-token down projection staged 8*2560*4 = 80 KB of dynamic
   shared memory, past the 64 KB workgroup LDS limit on RDNA3 (upstream targets RTX, where
   80 KB fits). hipFuncSetAttribute failed silently and the launch returned
   hipErrorInvalidValue, which killed the first prompt pass. 1024 divides D for the same
   tile count arithmetic; only the chunk count grows. No tolerance or math change.
2. The two argument-guard messages now print their values.
--- a/src/kernels/cuda/fused_gr.cu
+++ b/src/kernels/cuda/fused_gr.cu
@@ -178,7 +178,10 @@
     for (int i = t; i < D; i += THREADS) xn[i] *= s_rs[i / N];
 }
 
-constexpr int TILE = 2560;             // xn floats per token staged at a time: 320 chunks of 8, 10 per lane
+constexpr int TILE = 1024;  // rollout patch 0005: was 2560; 8 tokens * 2560 floats * 4 B = 80 KB of
+                            // dynamic LDS, past gfx1100's 64 KB workgroup limit (RTX cards allow it).
+                            // 1024 -> 32 KB; the tile loop below is exact for any TILE dividing D, so
+                            // the arithmetic is unchanged - only the chunk count grows (4 -> 10).             // xn floats per token staged at a time: 320 chunks of 8, 10 per lane
 constexpr int TQ = TILE / 8 / 32;      // uint4 weight chunks per lane per tile
 
